#front-title("Preface")

Somewhere, right now, someone is sitting before a black screen with nothing on it
but a small cursor blinking in silence. This book is written for that moment — and
for anyone standing at its threshold.

The only thing this book asks of you is that you can read and write. It assumes no
prior knowledge of computers or of Linux. We begin at absolute zero and build,
brick by brick, until you stand where the professionals stand.

#section[About this edition]

*From Zero to Root* is written Arabic‑first; this English edition is a faithful
mirror of the Arabic original. The command line is not a narrow skill — it is a
*key*: to commanding the machine instead of being commanded by it, and to the
infrastructure the modern world runs on.

And in the age of artificial intelligence, understanding these foundations matters
more, not less. AI sits *on top of* these systems, not in place of them: it acts
through the very terminal in your hands. Those who understand the foundation steer
the tool; those who don't remain passengers.

#note[
  The English edition is being written after the Arabic original matures. This is
